{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1753-gamblers-ruin-correlated-random-walks.md", "equation": "Increments {X_n} form a 2-state Markov chain (symmetric case: P(stay)=p=q). Gambler starts at 0, absorbed at −B (ruin) or A (success), τ = absorption time. Martingale approach: linear martingale M_n = (2−2p)S_n + (2p−1)X_n for ruin probability (OST); quadratic martingale M_n = S_n² + aS_nX_n − bn for expected duration. Extended to symmetric CRW with delays {1,0,−1} (§4), a martingale technique for general CRW with delays, and the two-arbitrary-pattern game (§5, e.g., HH vs TH: non-zero payments reduce to i.i.d. symmetric, α = (B−1/2)/(A+B)).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9136}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1753-gamblers-ruin-correlated-random-walks.md", "equation": "Sanity checks: A=B → α=1/2; p=1/2 (i.i.d.) → α=B/(A+B) (classical); p→1 → α→1/2 (first flip decides); B→∞ → α→1.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9136}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1753-gamblers-ruin-correlated-random-walks.md", "equation": "Expected duration (Eq. 4): E(τ) = (1/b)[b − (1+a) + A²α + B²β + a(Aα + Bβ)] with martingale coefficients a, b solved from the chain.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9136}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1753-gamblers-ruin-correlated-random-walks.md", "equation": "No numerical results. Exact formulas (2), (3), (4); the HH-vs-TH worked example (π_1=.25, p=q=1/2 → α=(B−1/2)/(A+B)).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9136}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1753-gamblers-ruin-correlated-random-walks.md", "equation": "Build the \"streak-aware ruin gate\": (a) from the engine's weekly settled P&L sign series, estimate p = P(win_t | win_{t−1}) (and the symmetric q) per market; (b) express bankroll in units of weekly stake; set A = target/profit-goal in units, B = bankroll in units; (c) compute α from Eq. (3); choose stake size so α ≤ 1% (or Garrett's tolerance); (d) recompute weekly as p drifts; (e) extend to {1,0,−1} using §4 to include push/no-bet weeks. Effort: ~0.5 day (estimator + formula + stake solver).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9136}
