{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1760-madness-multiple-entries-march-madness.md", "equation": "Field-aware EMS (fEMS):** the paper's EMS ignores the field. Extend the objective to P(best entry beats the field's best entry): model the field as K synthetic sharp entries (generated by running the same optimizer with perturbed projections), and maximize (1/N)Σ_n 𝟙[max_{e∈ℰ} s(e,ω_n) > max_{k} s(f_k,ω_n)]. Hypothesis: fEMS portfolios sacrifice raw EMS but gain win probability by differentiating from sharp-field lineups (contrarian leverage). Test: simulate against a synthetic sharp field on 2024 slates; success = fEMS portfolio wins ≥20% more often than plain-EMS portfolio with ≤3-point EMS loss.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9136}
